//! # `dSys` engine initialization - `0x800E48D0` and its immediate helpers
//!
//! ## What this module covers
//!
//! The one-time `dSys_c` start-up at `0x800E48D0` (640 bytes) plus the small
//! helpers in the same 0x800E45F0..0x800E52D0 cluster:
//!
//! | address | size | function here | role |
//! |---|---|---|---|
//! | `0x800E48D0` | 640 B | [`fn_800e48d0`] | create the root heaps and bring the subsystems up |
//! | `0x800E45F0` | 108 B | [`fn_800e45f0`] | allocate the 1 MiB / 2.5 MiB blocks |
//! | `0x800E4660` | 24 B | [`fn_800e4660`] | `dSys` mid-frame step (child `+0xC`) |
//! | `0x800E4680` | 84 B | [`fn_800e4680`] | `dSys` flag step (three bytes, child `+0x10`) |
//! | `0x800E46E0` | 72 B | [`fn_800e46e0`] | `dSys` begin-of-frame step |
//! | `0x800E4740` | 72 B | [`fn_800e4740`] | `dSys` end-of-frame step |
//! | `0x800E47A0` | 128 B | [`fn_800e47a0`] | flag/predicate helper on the `dSys` child |
//! | `0x800E4820` | 4 B | [`fn_800e4820`] | thunk to `0x8006A320` |
//! | `0x800E4830` | 24 B | [`fn_800e4830`] | byte setter on the `dSys` child (`+8`) |
//! | `0x800E4850` | 68 B | [`fn_800e4850`] | word setter on the `dSys` child (`+0x14`) |
//! | `0x800E48A0` | 40 B | [`fn_800e48a0`] | word getter from the `dSys` child (`+0x14`) |
//! | `0x800E5060` | 100 B | [`fn_800e5060`] | release the 1 MiB/2.5 MiB blocks and two objects |
//! | `0x800E5110` | 140 B | [`fn_800e5110`] | lazy 0xC800 object + its virtual release step |
//! | `0x800E51A0` | 92 B | [`fn_800e51a0`] | clamp the OS arena to the MEM1/MEM2 window |
//! | `0x800E5200` | 208 B | [`fn_800e5200`] | reset one heap/allocator object to a size |
//! | `0x800E52D0` | 96 B | [`fn_800e52d0`] | reset the three engine heap objects |
//! | `0x800E5400` | 128 B | [`fn_800e5400`] | construct the 0x18-entry `0x8031B194` object |
//! | `0x800E5480` | 88 B | [`fn_800e5480`] | destroy that object when the free count is positive |
//!
//! Wave 75 added three further clusters from the same `0x800E0000` bucket. They
//! are not part of the `dSys_c` start-up, but they sit directly above and below
//! it in the image and were the largest untranslated runs left at the time:
//!
//! | address range | count | role |
//! |---|---|---|
//! | `0x800E6930..0x800E71A0` | 14 | message-string builder: turns ids, counters and mode switches into the 0x10-slot wide string at `+4` |
//! | `0x800E7C70..0x800E8120` | 12 | tween/lerp helpers and the float field accessors of the `r13 - 0x5880` widget object |
//! | `0x800E8AB0..0x800E8F10` | 4 | display-metric capture and the 0x58-byte node chain of the list widget |
