// bytes. Every value was checked against the prologue and the closing `blr`:
// the last instruction of each body is a `bclr 20,0` that ends exactly four
// bytes before the next table entry (`0x800F2EAC`, `0x800F3330`, `0x800F33BC`,
// `0x800F3E74`, `0x800F4DA0`, `0x800F4F74`, `0x800F504C`, `0x800F5420`,
// `0x800F57D4`, `0x800F71B4`), so **none** of the ten sizes is a prologue
