// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 0x800F9370 - format the stage code
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// Formats the four-character stage code `"W<world><slot>"` for a stage index.
///
/// The body writes `'W'`, then the single world character (`'A'` when the world
/// argument is `9`, otherwise the argument plus `'1'`), then classifies the
/// stage index with [`fn_800f9840`] and fills the last two bytes from the
/// matching arm. Ten arms write one of the group letters `G`, `T`, `C`, `E`,
/// `W`, `A` or `S` plus a digit relative to the corresponding global edge word;
/// the `case 4` arm instead delegates to [`fn_800f9620`], which overwrites all
/// four bytes.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_800f9370` at `0x800F9370` (436 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/800f9370_FUN_800f9370.c`
/// - Extent: frame at `0x800F9370`, `blr` at `0x800F9520`, so
///   `0x800F9370..0x800F9524` - 436 bytes, the `functions.tsv` value (the next
///   twelve bytes are padding).
/// - observed: the dispatch is a `ctr` jump table of 11 words at `0x8031C0C0`
///   (`0x800F93D8`, `0x800F940C`, `0x800F9428`, `0x800F9448`, `0x800F9464`,
///   `0x800F9474`, `0x800F9490`, `0x800F94F8`, `0x800F94AC`, `0x800F94C8`,
///   `0x800F94E4`); the guard at `0x800F93B8` sends `r3 > 10` to the `0x800F94F8`
///   default. The ten arms, their letters and the global each one subtracts are
///   read from the disassembly rather than from the export's `switch`, whose
///   case labels are in a different order.
///
