/// * `param_1` - world number; `9` becomes `'A'`, everything else `+ '1'`.
/// * `param_2` - stage index, classified by [`fn_800f9840`] and printed.
/// * `param_3` - destination of the five-byte code (four characters plus the
///   terminator).
///
/// # Returns
/// `1` when a code was written, `0` for the default arm (classification `11`).
///
/// # Side effects
/// Up to five byte stores, or the [`fn_800f9620`] copy for `case 4`.
///
/// # Safety
/// `param_3 + 0..+5` must be writable and `param_2` must be a valid stage index.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - the jump table, the guard and every arm were read out of
/// `work/dol/main.elf`; the signed divide-by-ten of `case 0` is transcribed as
/// the `mulhw`/`srawi` quotient (Rust `/` truncates the same way).
