/// object): only `this != 0 && release > 0` runs `0x802B9280(this)`; the
/// receiver is returned either way. It sits directly after the float accessors
/// of the `r13 - 0x5880` widget object (`0x800E7C70..0x800E8120`), so it is the
/// cluster's deleting destructor.
