/// Emptiness of the scan sends control to the fallback. A non-empty scan is
/// used only when `+0x6D8` and the `+0xD` byte of its `+0x6D0` holder are both
/// non-zero; then [`fn_800f7a20`] runs. Every other path asks
/// [`fn_800f8c80`] and, when it accepts, calls [`fn_800f7ae0`].
///
/// # Original (untabled)
/// - Ghidra: none - no `functions.tsv` row and no export for `0x800F78F0`.
/// - Extent: `0x800F78F0..0x800F7964` (116 bytes, 29 words), ending at the
///   `blr` at `0x800F7960`; one zero word fills `0x800F7964..0x800F7968`.
/// - Reach: no `b`/`bl`; the only data word is `0x802F33D4`, the second word
///   of the `{0xFFFFFFFF, code, 0}` descriptor record at `0x802F33D0`. The
///   run is every third word, so the start is **not** a pointer-run interior
///   by the three-consecutive-word rule.
