///   `stw r31,0xC(r1)`; `mr r31,r3`; `bl 0x800F8B70`;
///   `cmpi cr0,r3,0`; `4182002C bc 12,2`; `lbz r0,0x6D8(r31)`;
///   `cmpi cr0,r0,0`; `41820020 bc 12,2`; `lwz r3,0x6D0(r31)`;
///   `lbz r0,0xD(r3)`; `cmpi cr0,r0,0`; `41820010 bc 12,2`;
///   `mr r3,r31`; `bl 0x800F7A20`; `b 0x800F7950`; fallback `mr r3,r31`;
///   `bl 0x800F8C80`; `cmpi cr0,r3,0`; `4182000C bc 12,2`;
///   `mr r3,r31`; `bl 0x800F7AE0`; epilogue; `4E800020 blr`.
/// - Polarity: every `4182xxxx` is `bc 12,2` (`bt cr0.eq`): an empty scan, a
///   zero `+0x6D8`, a zero `+0xD` or a zero fallback answer all **skip** the
///   guarded call. The final `b` exits after the state-2 arm.
/// - Decoder note: `0x800F8B70` is a 16-byte tail call to
///   `fn_800f6d60(this, 0x802F3408, 5)`; the Rust calls the same translated
///   callee directly so the scan's `r3` result stays available.
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `this` - sequence object (`r31`).
